<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="NEXUS TwinLoop Legal Lab v3.3 — an experimental legal AI safety and retrieval architecture."
    />

    <title>Legal AI Lab — AiLawyer.world</title>

    <style>
      :global(*) {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      :global(html) {
        background: #07111f;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: #07111f;
        color: #f3f7fb;
        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      }

      .container {
        width: min(1000px, 90%);
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 3rem 0 6rem;
      }

      .back {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
        color: #47d7ff;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .back:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        color: #47d7ff;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      }

      h1 {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
        font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 8vw, 5.5rem);
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
      }

      .lead {
        max-width: 760px;
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        color: #b8c5d4;
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .badges {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
      }

      .badge {
        padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid #47d7ff;
        border-radius: 999px;
        color: #47d7ff;
        font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      }

      h2 {
        margin: 3.5rem 0 1.25rem;
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .architecture,
      .metrics {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
      }

      .card {
        padding: 1.5rem;
        border: 1px solid #203248;
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        background: #0b1728;
      }

      .card h3 {
        margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
        color: #f3f7fb;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
      }

      .card p {
        margin: 0;
        color: #9eacbd;
        line-height: 1.65;
      }

      .metric-value {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        color: #47d7ff;
        font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
        font-size: 2rem;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .metric-name {
        color: #b8c5d4;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }

      .coverage {
        border-color: #e49a3a;
      }

      .coverage .metric-value {
        color: #e49a3a;
      }

      .note {
        margin-top: 2rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        border-left: 4px solid #e49a3a;
        background: #111d2e;
        color: #b8c5d4;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .disclaimer {
        margin-top: 3rem;
        padding-top: 1.5rem;
        border-top: 1px solid #203248;
        color: #8493a6;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      @media (max-width: 700px) {
        .architecture,
        .metrics {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="container">
      <a class="back" href="/">← Back to home</a>

      <p class="eyebrow">EXPERIMENTAL LEGAL AI LAB</p>

      <h1>NEXUS TwinLoop Legal Lab v3.3</h1>

      <p class="lead">
        A laboratory prototype for testing retrieval quality, unsupported
        claims, jurisdiction boundaries, service limitations, and high-risk
        legal scenarios.
      </p>

      <div class="badges">
        <span class="badge">STATUS: LAB PROTOTYPE</span>
        <span class="badge">SOURCE GUARD: ACTIVE</span>
        <span class="badge">PRODUCTION: NO</span>
      </div>

      <h2>Architecture</h2>

      <section class="architecture">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Active / Shadow loops</h3>
          <p>
            Two evaluation paths support controlled comparison before a model
            or retrieval configuration is promoted.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Source-controlled generation</h3>
          <p>
            The prototype is designed to answer from retrieved material and
            return an unverified state when support is insufficient.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Jurisdiction detection</h3>
          <p>
            The system checks whether a relevant jurisdiction has been
            identified before allowing jurisdiction-specific conclusions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Boundary detection</h3>
          <p>
            Requests involving representation, filing, guaranteed outcomes, or
            unsupported professional services are detected and refused.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <h2>Current test metrics</h2>

      <section class="metrics">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="metric-value">0%</span>
          <div class="metric-name">Unsupported claim rate</div>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="metric-value">100%</span>
          <div class="metric-name">Service-boundary refusal rate</div>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="metric-value">100%</span>
          <div class="metric-name">Jurisdiction-boundary rate</div>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="metric-value">100%</span>
          <div class="metric-name">Out-of-scope refusal rate</div>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="metric-value">100%</span>
          <div class="metric-name">Legal detection accuracy</div>
        </article>

        <article class="card coverage">
          <span class="metric-value">24%</span>
          <div class="metric-name">Retrieval coverage rate</div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <aside class="note">
        The 24% retrieval coverage reflects the intentionally small placeholder
        corpus used in the laboratory test. It is reported openly as a retrieval
        limitation and should not be interpreted as a production-readiness
        score.
      </aside>

      <p class="disclaimer">
        This laboratory prototype is not a legal service, does not provide legal
        representation, and is not ready for production use.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>